## 🧪 Data Processing and Template Selection

BLASTp results from multiple proteins were aggregated into a unified dataset using a custom Python pipeline. Each alignment entry included query ID, subject ID, percent identity, alignment length, and a computed similarity score.

The similarity score was calculated as:

similarity_score = (percent identity × alignment length) / 100

This metric integrates both sequence identity and alignment coverage to prioritize structurally relevant templates.

Proteins were classified into modeling strategies based on sequence identity:
- >35% identity → Homology modeling (MODELLER)
- ≤35% identity → Threading (I-TASSER)

For each protein, the highest scoring template was selected for downstream structural modeling.

Data processing and filtering were performed using Python.
